      why_finanz: 'Account and card numbers together with a name are enough for fraud such as fake direct debits or purchases.',
      why_sozial: 'Social security numbers stay with a person for life and make identity theft easier.',
      why_gesundheit: 'Health data – insurance numbers, diagnoses, medication – is treated by law as particularly sensitive.',
      why_firma: 'Company identifiers and internal terms reveal which customers, partners or projects are involved.',
      why_kontakt: 'Email addresses, phone numbers and dates of birth identify people and make targeted phishing easier.',
      why_steuer: 'Tax IDs are assigned to a person permanently and are misused for tax and identity fraud.',
      why_technik: 'Anyone who knows a key or token can often access systems or data with it directly.',
      'why_id-national': 'National ID numbers are assigned to a person permanently and make identity theft easier.',
      why_person: 'Identity, HR details, beliefs and whole customer lists make people identifiable – the law protects them specially.',
      why_reise: 'Passport and ID card data are often enough to open accounts or pose as someone else.',
      learn_finanz: 'An IBAN tells others where money can be collected from; with the account holder\'s name, fake direct debits and convincing payment requests become possible. Card numbers with expiry date or security code are enough for online purchases.',
      learn_sozial: 'Social security numbers such as the Swiss AHV number cannot simply be changed. Combined with a name and date of birth they help others pose as the person towards authorities, insurers or employers.',
      learn_gesundheit: 'Health insurance numbers, diagnoses, ICD codes and medication linked to a person reveal health information. Health data is a special category under data protection law (Swiss FADP, EU GDPR) and needs particular care. General questions without a recognisable person (e.g. "What is diabetes?") are not flagged.',
      learn_firma: 'VAT and company numbers are often public, but in a chat they show whom you are working with. Custom terms from your organisation (customer names, project code names) can reveal confidential business relationships.',
      learn_kontakt: 'Contact details identify people. In AI chats they often end up in texts that are stored with the provider; attackers use such details for targeted phishing.',
      learn_steuer: 'Tax IDs such as the German tax identification number or the Italian codice fiscale stay the same for life. They are used for tax returns and refunds and are therefore attractive for fraud.',
      learn_technik: 'Passwords, API keys, tokens and private keys grant access without further checks. Once a key has been sent, treat it as compromised: revoke it and create a new one.',
      'learn_id-national': 'National ID numbers (e.g. Belgium, the Netherlands) are used across authorities, banks and health care. A leaked number cannot easily be replaced.',
      learn_person: 'Name, date of birth and address together identify a person. Dismissals, salaries and appraisals as well as religion, political views or union membership of a named person are particularly sensitive (Swiss FADP Art. 5, EU GDPR Art. 9). A list with many e-mail addresses, phone numbers or IBANs is usually a customer or staff export and does not belong in an AI chat. Only text that refers to a recognisable person is flagged.',
      learn_reise: 'The machine-readable zone and the number of passports and ID cards contain name, date of birth and document number. Such data is used to open accounts and for identity fraud.',
